    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8b0a2f4f_ccdf41e9",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiStateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 5193,
      "author": {
        "id": 1086611
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-02T18:38:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "First of all, we still have to handle devices that don\u0027t support this new roaming feature. There we send a CMD_START_CONNECT directly and drive supplicant to make the connection. Here for CMD_STOP_FW_ROAMING_AND_CONNECT we have to handle the case that stopping fw roaming returned ERROR_BUSY and we have to wait for the roaming completion notice then drive supplicant to make the connection.\n\nBasically I\u0027d like to keep CMD_START_CONNECT as is such that it always make the connection attempt and let CMD_STOP_FW_ROAMING_AND_CONNECT worry about wait, start watchdog, and etc. I think it is a cleaner design.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5193,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 5193,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "4905d234c1feabe9764a0223079e35f7ddb66105",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ddd3488f_8a0c9b96",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiStateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 5193,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-03T05:46:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As I understand the code, a device will either have firmware roaming supported or not, it isn\u0027t going to change settings while running on an interface.  If that assumption is correct, then you are either going to be doing CMD_START_CONNECT calls or you will be doing CMD_STOP_FW_ROAMING_AND_CONNECT messages.  You do not need support in both.\nIf both types of messages can be sent for a single running instance of WifiStateMachine, then please explain how that can happen (other than the calls you added in this CL).",
      "parentUuid": "8b0a2f4f_ccdf41e9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5193,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 5193,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "4905d234c1feabe9764a0223079e35f7ddb66105",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
